    page=f'<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>Trade Dashboard</title>{styles}</head><body><main><header><div><div class="eyebrow">Project Atlas · Risk & validation review</div><h1>Trade Dashboard</h1><p>Controlled-risk objective: 25–40% annual net return · Maximum drawdown below 10%<br>December 15, 2025 – October 30, 2026 · 320 calendar days · USD</p></div><span class="badge">PAPER ONLY · FROZEN RULES</span></header><div class="alert"><strong>Decision: retain paper-only status.</strong> The modeled ledgers reconcile, but the $500 recovery portfolio remains above 10% drawdown. Untouched out-of-sample and genuine walk-forward results are unavailable. Annual performance and repeatability are unverified. The $25 planned-risk ceiling does not guarantee a $25 realized-loss limit: one higher-cost exit lost $42.35.</div><div class="cards"><div class="card"><small>Improved ending balance · standard</small><div class="metric">{money(recovery["ending_balance"])}</div><small class="positive">{money(recovery["net_pnl"],True)} · modeled after costs</small></div><div class="card"><small>Observed win rate</small><div class="metric">{recovery["win_rate"]:.2f}%</div><small>{recovery["outcomes"]} closed trades · reused history</small></div><div class="card"><small>Maximum intratrade drawdown</small><div class="metric negative">{recovery["quote_marked_drawdown_pct"]:.2f}%</div><small>Higher costs: {higher["quote_marked_drawdown_pct"]:.2f}% · target &lt;10%</small></div><div class="card"><small>Untouched OOS / walk-forward</small><div class="metric">N/A</div><small>Blocked · no eligible unseen cohort</small></div></div>'
    page+='<section><h2>Original, benchmark and recovery-filter comparison</h2>'+table(['System','Costs','Ending balance','Net P&L','Period return','Win rate','Quote DD','Trades'],totals)+'<p class="note">Original: NAS 5m both directions. Benchmark: NAS 5m short-only. Improved: benchmark plus NAS 15m prior-20-bar directional efficiency ≥0.30 only after two negative NAS exits. SPX 15m and NAS 15m retain 1.5R; NAS 5m retains native RSI exits. All use one shared $500 account and $25 planned total open risk, with $10 recovery risk. The recovery filter removes exactly one development-period loss under each cost model; later fills are unchanged.</p></section>'
