    page+='<section><h2>Performance statistics · net modeled results</h2>'+table(['Metric']+[LABELS[r['system']]+' / '+r['scenario'] for r in core],metrics_rows)+'<p class="note">¹ Requested annualization = (ending/starting balance)<sup>365.2425/320</sup>−1. This extrapolates less than one year and is not an actual annual return or forecast. <a href="https://www.gipsstandards.org/standards/gips-standards-for-firms/gips-standards-handbook-for-firms/">GIPS guidance</a> does not permit annualized sub-year performance claims; this report makes no compliance claim.<br>² Daily returns use all Mon–Fri, idle/holiday zeros, 252 annualization, risk-free rate and downside target both zero. Sharpe uses sample standard deviation. Sortino uses sqrt(mean(min(return,0)²)) across all days. Assumptions and serial dependence limit interpretation; see <a href="https://web.stanford.edu/~wfsharpe/art/sr/sr.htm">Sharpe’s original discussion</a>. Average loss is signed; profit factor uses positive net profits divided by absolute negative net profits.</p></section>'
    page+='<section><h2>Untouched out-of-sample and walk-forward status</h2>'+table(['Evaluation','Result','Trades / return / DD','Reason'],[['Untouched out-of-sample','NOT RUN','N/A','No eligible unexposed broker executable period'],['Genuine walk-forward','NOT RUN','N/A','Historical dates already used for model selection'],['Chronological stability cohorts','Completed · reused','See below','Frozen rules, no optimization; not OOS']])+'<p>June–October is not independent validation. Earlier H1/H4 seasonal work also exposed older market periods. Read-only probes returned no June/November quotes; the December 11 sample is additional detail on overlapping history. Different-instrument IBKR index bars cannot validate the broker CFD bid/ask execution model.</p><details><summary>Frozen prospective validation protocol</summary><p>Collect genuinely new completed sessions after this audit freeze with receipt timestamps and raw hashes. Keep the original, benchmark and recovery rules frozen in parallel paper books. Report consecutive 20-session folds with continuous cash and recovery state; do not refit on fold results. At least one full unseen year and 100 portfolio trades, adequate lane samples and verified costs/clock/margin are required before assessing the annual target. No collector or schedule has been activated by this report.</p></details></section>'
    page+='<section><h2>Individual strategies · separate $500 paper accounts</h2>'+table(['Lane','Costs','Net P&L','Win rate','Trades','Quote DD','PF','Sharpe','Sortino','Expectancy','Avg win','Avg loss','Max loss streak'],individ)+'<p class="note">Standalone accounts do not compete for capital. Their results must not be added to infer the shared account. Portfolio contributions use actual shared allocations and are available in the complete ledgers. † Fewer than10 negative weekdays: Sortino is unstable. The NAS5short standard ratio is extremely high because almost all daily net returns are nonnegative despite individual losing trades;do not treat it as reliable strategy superiority. All individual Nasdaq trade samples remain small.</p></section>'
    page+='<section><details><summary>Strategy contributions within the shared account</summary>'+table(['System','Costs','Lane','Attributed net P&L','Trades','Win rate','Net PF'],attributed)+'<p class="note">Each row uses the fills actually admitted to the common account. Net contributions sum to portfolio P&L. These differ from standalone accounts because of shared risk and margin limits.</p></details><details><summary>Overlapping trade pairs · recovery portfolio</summary>'+table(['Costs','Pair','Overlapping pairs','Both ended at a loss','Overlap minutes'],overlap)+'<p class="note">Pairs use intersecting holding intervals and their final trade outcomes;they are not losses measured only during the overlap. Very little simultaneous exposure and few jointly active days prevent a strong diversification conclusion.</p></details></section>'
    page+='<section><h2>Correlated losses and portfolio exposure</h2><p>NAS100 / SPX500 daily RTH close-return correlation: <strong>'+fmt(market['daily_close_return_correlation'])+'</strong> across '+str(market['return_observations'])+' common complete-session return observations. This is market dependence, not proof of strategy diversification.</p>'+table(['Costs','Strategy pair','Daily P&L correlation','Both active days','Both losing days','Combined P&L on co-loss days'],correlation)+table(['System','Costs','Max gross notional','Max gross / equity','Max planned open risk','Max risk / equity','Max positions','Max reserved margin','Overlap minutes'],exposure)+table(['System','Costs','Max held-mark quote age','Losses beyond planned risk','Largest actual modeled loss','Total excess loss beyond plan'],qualityrows)+'<p class="note">Gross notional can be large despite a fixed stop-risk budget. Stops do not cap losses through gaps, latency or unavailable liquidity. Mark quote-age is not verified order latency or executable depth. Per-pair jointly active samples are small. Daily P&L correlations include zero weekdays; simultaneous loss/holding pairs and marked exposure are recorded in supporting results. Gross margin receives no hedge credit.</p></section>'
    page+='<section><h2>Cost and execution stress · frozen rules, no selection</h2>'+table(['Scenario','System','Net P&L','Quote DD','Win rate','Trades','Max planned risk','Max margin'],stressrows)+'<p class="note">Single factors: spread2×; commission$18 roundtrip/lot;4 adverse ticks each side; entry5 seconds later; exit instruction delayed1 second; margin2×. Combined severe applies all. Standard: spread1×,fee$6,slip1tick; higher:1.5×,$12,2ticks. Exit-delay scenario models market-if-touch execution on the first subsequent own-symbol quote after delay, including gap risk. Every rejected/unaffordable entry is retained. These scenarios are estimates, not verified broker execution.</p></section>'
    page+='<section><h2>Below 10% drawdown · capital normalization, not refitting</h2><p>The unchanged $500 system does not meet the below-10% requirement. The entry-delay sensitivity did cross below10% in this historical sample, but that is not an independently validated improvement and was not selected as a new rule. Timing sensitivity is a reason to preserve the benchmark and seek fresh evidence.</p><p>One risk-only illustration keeps exactly the same $500 trading sleeve and fills, plus $750 segregated cash unavailable to margin or sizing. Total capital is $1,250, so the $25 planned ceiling is 2% of initial total capital. The reserve amount follows this risk fraction; it was not searched against trade outcomes.</p>'+table(['System','Costs','Initial total capital','Ending total capital','Period return','Annual extrapolation¹','Quote DD'],overlay)+'<p class="note">This is arithmetic on unchanged fills, with reserve interest zero. It requires additional capital and lowers return on total capital; it does not create trading edge or demonstrate that future drawdown stays below10%. Minimum lot increments can prevent equivalent risk reduction in a $500 account. No funds were moved and no account/risk controls changed. Broker costs and future adverse regimes can still invalidate the target.</p></section>'
    page+='<section><details><summary>Chronological fixed-rule cohorts · contaminated stability diagnostic</summary>'+table(['Costs','Window','Net P&L','Trades','Win rate','Within-cohort quote DD','Classification'],cohort)+'<p class="note">Cash and recovery state carry across cohorts; drawdown restarts its measurement peak at cohort entry. Cohort returns are not independent or optimized. Sparse later activity cannot establish seasonal reliability.</p></details></section>'
    page+='<section><h2>Complete modeled cost reconciliation</h2>'+table(['System','Costs','Commission','Adverse slippage','Embedded spread proxy','All intraday','Largest P&L formula error'],costrows)+'<p class="note">Commission and slippage are already embedded in net figures; do not deduct again. The spread column is an embedded bid-reference proxy, not a separate debit or a complete zero-cost counterfactual, especially at capped target fills. No positions held overnight in audited runs, so modeled rollover/swap is zero. Historical minimum fees, financing rules, platform charges, taxes, currency conversion and liquidity/queue behavior are not verified. Reported “net” means net of the specified modeled trading costs, not every business expense. Higher costs can change affordability,recovery and subsequent fills,so cost paths need not be monotonic.</p><p class="note">The model retains fractional cents,including half-cent amounts created by stressed spreads. Tables round for display;the sum of displayed rows can differ by cents from the rounded full-precision total. Static per-trade cent-rounding differences are recorded separately. Actual broker fee and currency rounding are unverified.</p><p class="note"><a href="https://lhfx.com/faqs">Current LHFX FAQ</a> describes$6 roundtrip/lot for Standard and$7 for Islamic accounts. It does not verify this account’s historical fee schedule or account type. <a href="https://www.mql5.com/en/docs/python_metatrader5/mt5copyticksrange_py">MT5’s Python documentation</a> describes UTC timestamps; the existing empirical broker shift remains conditional pending dated account evidence.</p></section>'
    page+='<section><h2>Verified versus estimated</h2><div class="wrap">'+table(['Item','Evidence status','Scope and limitation'],verification)+'</div></section>'
    page+='<section><h2>Complete trade ledger</h2><div class="controls"><label for="ledgersystem">System </label><select id="ledgersystem"><option value="recovery">Improved recovery filter</option><option value="benchmark">Pre-filter benchmark</option><option value="original">Original system</option></select><label for="ledgercost">Costs </label><select id="ledgercost"><option value="standard">Standard</option><option value="higher">Higher</option></select><button id="downloadledger">Download JSON ledger</button><span id="ledgercount" class="note"></span></div><div id="ledgertable" class="ledger scroll" style="margin-top:16px"></div><p class="note">Times shown in New York under the existing inferred clock. Entry, exit, quantity, initial stop, target, net P&L, planned risk and reason are all available. No actual brokerage account identifiers or balances are included.</p></section>'
    page+='<section><h2>Reproducibility</h2><p>30 audit runs,6 exact archived portfolio matches,16 independent quote reconstructions,110 software checks. Input/model/record hashes, scenario protocol, complete ledgers, admission decisions, verification register and validation status are included in the local bundle. Quote-level traces remain local and are excluded from the portable download.</p><code>Protocol SHA-256: '+hashlib.sha256((out/'protocol.json').read_bytes()).hexdigest()+'<br>Results SHA-256: '+hashlib.sha256((out/'results.json').read_bytes()).hexdigest()+'</code></section><div class="footer"><span class="note">Project Atlas · Paper-only · No strategy optimization or live orders</span><span class="note">Audit generated '+summary['generated_utc']+'</span></div>'
    page+='<script type="application/json" id="auditdata">'+json.dumps(payload,allow_nan=False).replace('</','<\\/')+'</script>'
    page+='''<script>
    const D=JSON.parse(document.getElementById('auditdata').textContent),$=s=>document.getElementById(s),cash=x=>x==null?'—':new Intl.NumberFormat('en-US',{style:'currency',currency:'USD'}).format(x),num=x=>x==null?'—':Number(x).toFixed(2),ny=t=>new Date(t*1000).toLocaleString('en-US',{timeZone:'America/New_York',year:'numeric',month:'2-digit',day:'2-digit',hour:'2-digit',minute:'2-digit',hour12:false});
    function plot(){let cost=$('chartcost').value,rs=D.rows.filter(r=>r.scenario===cost),values=rs.flatMap(r=>[500,...r.metrics.daily_balance]),lo=Math.min(...values)-15,hi=Math.max(...values)+15,W=900,H=280,colors={original:'#8aa7d4',benchmark:'#b89be4',recovery:'#65ddba'},s='';for(let j=0;j<5;j++){let v=lo+(hi-lo)*j/4,y=H-25-j*(H-50)/4;s+=`<line x1="66" y1="${y}" x2="880" y2="${y}" stroke="#26384f"/><text x="8" y="${y+4}" fill="#91a8c2" font-size="11">${cash(v)}</text>`}for(let r of rs){let a=[500,...r.metrics.daily_balance],p=a.map((v,i)=>`${66+i*814/(a.length-1)},${H-25-(v-lo)/(hi-lo)*(H-50)}`).join(' ');s+=`<polyline points="${p}" fill="none" stroke="${colors[r.system]}" stroke-width="2.3"/>`}$('balanceplot').innerHTML=s;let r=rs.find(r=>r.system==='recovery'),a=r.audit.curve,m=Math.max(10,r.quote_marked_drawdown_pct)*1.12,t0=a[0].t,t1=a[a.length-1].t,p=a.map(v=>`${45+(v.t-t0)/(t1-t0)*385},${25+v.drawdown_pct/m*220}`).join(' '),line=25+10/m*220;$('ddplot').innerHTML=`<line x1="45" x2="430" y1="${line}" y2="${line}" stroke="#f2cc83" stroke-dasharray="5,5"/><text x="8" y="${line+4}" fill="#f2cc83" font-size="11">10%</text><polyline points="${p}" fill="none" stroke="#ff8c9c" stroke-width="1.6"/><text x="45" y="17" fill="#91a8c2" font-size="11">Peak-to-trough decline · ${cost} costs</text>`}
    function ledger(){let key=$('ledgersystem').value+'_'+$('ledgercost').value,a=D.ledgers[key];$('ledgercount').textContent=a.length+' closed trades · net '+cash(a.reduce((v,f)=>v+f.pnl,0));$('ledgertable').innerHTML='<table><thead><tr>'+['#','Lane','Entry NY','Exit NY','Side','Lots','Entry','Exit','Stop','Target','Net P&L','Planned risk','Reason'].map(s=>'<th>'+s+'</th>').join('')+'</tr></thead><tbody>'+a.map((f,i)=>`<tr><td>${i+1}</td><td>${f.strategy}</td><td>${ny(f.entry_at)}</td><td>${ny(f.exit_at)}</td><td>${f.side===1?'Long':'Short'}</td><td>${num(f.quantity)}</td><td>${num(f.entry)}</td><td>${num(f.exit)}</td><td>${num(f.stop)}</td><td>${num(f.target)}</td><td class="${f.pnl>=0?'positive':'negative'}">${cash(f.pnl)}</td><td>${cash(f.planned_risk)}</td><td>${f.reason}</td></tr>`).join('')+'</tbody></table>'}
    $('chartcost').addEventListener('change',plot);$('ledgersystem').addEventListener('change',ledger);$('ledgercost').addEventListener('change',ledger);$('downloadledger').addEventListener('click',()=>{let k=$('ledgersystem').value+'_'+$('ledgercost').value,u=URL.createObjectURL(new Blob([JSON.stringify(D.ledgers[k],null,2)],{type:'application/json'})),a=document.createElement('a');a.href=u;a.download='Atlas_'+k+'_ledger.json';a.click();setTimeout(()=>URL.revokeObjectURL(u),1000)});plot();ledger();
    </script></main></body></html>'''
    # Visible interface respects the existing title/wording preference.
    assert not re.search(r'\b(demo|test)\b',re.sub(r'<script[\s\S]*?</script>','',re.sub(r'<style[\s\S]*?</style>','',page)),re.I)
    (out/'report.html').write_text(page,encoding='utf-8')
    md=['Project Atlas audit — paper only','Period:Dec15,2025-Oct30,2026;320calendar days. Initial500USD.','Original/benchmark/recovery ledgers reconcile understandard/highercosts. Actualannualreturn,untouchedOOS andgenuinewalk-forward remainunverified/unavailable. RecoveryDD10.99/11.57 exceeds10percent. Fullmetrics/scenarios/ledgers areinreport.html andresults.json.','Prospectiveprotocol andverificationregister explicitly separateverifiedarithmetic fromestimatedeconomics. Allbenchmarks preserved;nooptimization orliveorders.']
    (out/'README.txt').write_text('\n\n'.join(md),encoding='utf-8');archive=root/'outputs/downloads/Project_Atlas_Risk_Audit_v1.zip'
    with ZipFile(archive,'w',ZIP_DEFLATED) as z:
        z.write(out/'report.html','Trade Dashboard.html');z.write(out/'README.txt','README.txt')
        for f in out.rglob('*'):
            if f.is_file() and f.suffix!='.npz' and 'dist' not in f.relative_to(out).parts and f.name not in ('report.html','README.txt'):z.write(f,'supporting_records/'+f.relative_to(out).as_posix())
    with ZipFile(archive) as z:assert z.testzip() is None
    print(json.dumps(dict(report=str(out/'report.html'),archive=str(archive),cases=30,OOS='blocked',walkforward='blocked',market_correlation=market)))


